    "response": "{\n  \"decision\": \"no_flaw_established\",\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ISSUE_0001\",\n      \"category\": \"contextual_flattening\",\n      \"target_kind\": \"assertion\",\n      \"claim_quote\": \"Every displayed source presents the same severe and unresolved version of policy debate.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"excerpt_id\": \"EXC_04acb0787dcd5fee\",\n          \"quote\": \"My constituents were caught up in the chaos on the east coast main line on the 27th, like so many others. They recall poor communication not just during their journey but in advance of it, for planning purposes. They were, of course, also caught up in the Finsbury Park chaos and held around Stevenage for anything up to two hours. What can the Secretary of State do to ensure that communication is improved and our public transport network is properly operational throughout holiday periods?\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"whole_packet_no_support\": \"The evidence focuses on specific instances of communication failures and disruptions, without establishing a uniform 'severe and unresolved version of policy debate' across all sources.\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"divergent_accounts\",\n      \"material_consequence\": \"The evidence presents multiple accounts of events, indicating a lack of a single, universally agreed-upon 'severe and unresolved version'.\",\n      \"counterconditions\": \"The evidence demonstrates a range of issues and responses, not a single, consistent narrative.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ISSUE_0002\",\n      \"category\": \"unsupported_inference\",\n      \"target_kind\": \"assertion\",\n      \"claim_quote\": \"Every displayed source presents the same severe and unresolved version of policy debate.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"excerpt_id\": \"EXC_0c13531aa1f035c8\",\n          \"quote\": \"I do not want to keep on repeating myself. I have talked about the necessity of doing these big engineering projects over what is usually the less busy period, as opposed to creating the scale of disruption that would occur if they were done in the normal working week or at other times of the year. We will need to look at this; some of the suggestions from my right hon. Friend the Member for Saffron Walden (Sir Alan Haselhurst) made that clear. On communications, I wholly agree with the hon. Gentleman: the communications were not up to scratch in any way, shape or form, and the whole industry has got to try to address that.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"whole_packet_no_support\": \"The evidence describes a need to address communication issues, but does not establish a shared 'severe and unresolved version of policy debate'.\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"assumption_of_agreement\",\n      \"material_consequence\": \"The evidence does not support the claim that all sources share a common understanding or assessment of the situation.\",\n      \"counterconditions\": \"The evidence highlights differing opinions and approaches to the problem.\"\n    }\n  ],\"unresolved\": [],\"rationale\":\"The evidence presented describes a range of specific issues and responses related to transport disruptions, but does not provide a single, unified account or assessment of the 'policy debate' as claimed in the original statement. The evidence demonstrates divergent accounts and perspectives, making it impossible to definitively state that all sources present the same 'severe and unresolved version'. The identified issues relate to contextual flattening and unsupported inference.\"}",
    "done": true,
    "done_reason": "stop",
